Chapter: BvtResidentUnbind
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtResidentFall
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 UOAIX-143 (trial 43060, owner row 26 serial 2152): cg-deaths unbinds non-residents before the residents fall. Answers
 the resident's person index times 100, plus 1 when its owner row is held before, 2 when it falls through the cg-deaths
 order (cg-unbind-person, then cg-residents-fall), 4 when its row is then gone; negative when not buildable.
  bru-checks : Integer -> Integer
  bru-checks (k) = when brf-founded 0
    is Err (_) -> 0 - 1
    is Ok (owner) -> when owner.town
      is None -> 0 - 2
      is Just (t) -> if t.count <= k then 0 - 3
        else let r = list-at t.residents k
        in let serial = (tf-person t.people r.person).world-serial
        in let v = owner.vendor
        in let held = gv-owner v serial 0 >= 0
        in let unbound = cg-unbind-person t serial 1
        in let fell = cg-residents-fall t serial 0
        in r.person * 100 + (if held then 1 else 0) + (if fell == 1 then 2 else 0) + (if gv-owner v serial 0 < 0 then 4 else 0)
  bvt-resident-unbind : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-resident-unbind (unused) = act
    a0 <- bru-checks 0
    a1 <- bru-checks 1
    a2 <- bru-checks 2
    bvt-check ("every resident killed through the cg-deaths order loses its owner row (UOAIX-143, trial 43060; codes " & show a0 & " " & show a1 & " " & show a2 & ")") (int-mod a0 100 == 7 & int-mod a1 100 == 7 & int-mod a2 100 == 7)
  end
